            <ArticleTitle>[Effect of heparin and pelentan on the biopolymer metabolism of connective tissue in myocardial infarct].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>44-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The levels of free and peptide-bound hydroxyproline, hexosamines, glycosaminoglycans and elastolytic blood plasma activity were found to be altered in patients with myocardial infarction. The shifts in these indicators depended on the disease standing and the type of anticoagulant therapy.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
